#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:37
msgid ""
"Generally Primes are preferred over zooms in video. (Some people, prefer it "
"over zooms as well for photography — but this is a matter of taste and of "
"how you work.) Why is that? A psychological reason is that eyes cannot zoom "
"either, so zooming is hardly ever used in video. The technical reason is "
"that Primes are cheaper to build whilst offering better quality: Better "
"sharpness, bigger aperture (for limiting the :abbr:`DOF (Depth of Field)`). "
"Opening the aperture gives you a very nice look."
msgstr ""
"Vo všeobecnosti sa v oblasti videa uprednostňujú pevné objektívy pred "
"zoomami. (Niektorí ľudia ich uprednostňujú pred zoomami aj pri fotografii — "
"to je však otázka vkusu a spôsobu práce.) Prečo je tomu tak? Psychologickým "
"dôvodom je, že ani ľudské oči nevedia priblížovať, takže zoom sa vo videu "
"takmer vôbec nepoužíva. Technickým dôvodom je, že pevné objektívy sú "
"lacnejšie na výrobu a zároveň ponúkajú lepšiu kvalitu: lepšiu ostrosť, väčší "
"otvor clony (pre obmedzenie :abbr:`DOF (Depth of Field)`). Otvorenie clony "
"vám dáva veľmi pekný vizuálny efekt."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:39
msgid ""
"Examples for very popular primes are the Nikon 50mm f/1.8D and the Canon "
"50mm f/1.8 II."
msgstr ""
"Príkladmi veľmi obľúbených pevných objektívov sú Nikon 50mm f/1.8D a Canon "
"50mm f/1.8 II."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:41
msgid ""
"If you own such a lens, just do not forget that you should not always shoot "
"at f/1.8. ;)"
msgstr ""
"Ak vlastníte takýto objektív, nezabudnite, že by ste nemali vždy natáčať pri "
"f/1.8. ;)"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:44
msgid "Filter"
msgstr "Filter"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:51
msgid ""
":abbr:`NDF (Neutral Density Filter)` (the piece of kneaded eraser is not "
"part of the filter)"
msgstr ""
":abbr:`NDF (Neutral Density Filter)` (kúsok plastickej gumy nie je súčasťou "
"filtra)"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:53
msgid ""
"Directly related to the previous point about lenses. Shooting with an open "
"aperture works well as long as it is dark. In bright sunlight it will fail "
"because there is too much light falling on the sensor. Furthermore you are "
"forced to use a high shutter speed which makes movements look jerky; Most of "
"the time you will want to have some kind of motion blur because it looks "
"more natural to our eyes."
msgstr ""
"Priamo súvisí s predchádzajúcim bodom o objektívoch. Natáčanie s otvorenou "
"clonou funguje dobre, pokiaľ je tma. V jasnom slnečnom svetle to zlyhá, "
"pretože na snímač dopadá príliš veľa svetla. Okrem toho ste nútení používať "
"vysokú rýchlosť uzávierky, čo spôsobuje trhané pohyby; väčšinou budete "
"chcieť mať nejaké rozmazanie pohybu, pretože to vyzerá prirodzenejšie pre "
"naše oči."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:55
msgid ""
"If you ever tried to follow a bird or another animal with your eyes in dawn, "
"you will know that our eyes do support motion blur."
msgstr ""
"Ak ste sa niekedy pokúsili sledovať vtáka alebo iné zviera očami za súmraku, "
"viete, že naše oči rozmazanie pohybu skutočne vnímajú."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:57
msgid ""
"So the trick is to remove some light with a filter called Neutral Density "
"Filter."
msgstr ""
"Trik teda spočíva v tom, že sa čiastočne odstráni svetlo pomocou filtra "
"nazývaného filter neutrálnej hustoty."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:61
msgid "Shooting"
msgstr "Fotenie"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:64
msgid "Aperture, Shutter, and ISO"
msgstr "Clona, uzávierka a ISO"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:66
msgid "|pic3|  |pic4|"
msgstr "|pic3|  |pic4|"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:68
msgid "pic3"
msgstr "pic3"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:71
msgid "pic4"
msgstr "pic4"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:74
msgid ""
"The same as for shooting stills. Really? Not quite. As written above you "
"will usually want to have the shutter speed lower than for photography in "
"order to get motion blur — around 1/50 s. (This is just a rule of thumb, as "
"all rules in video are - made to be broken.)"
msgstr ""
"Rovnako ako pri fotografovaní statických záberov. Naozaj? Nie celkom. Ako je "
"uvedené vyššie, zvyčajne budete chcieť mať rýchlosť uzávierky nižšiu ako pri "
"fotografii, aby ste dosiahli rozmazanie pohybu — okolo 1/50 s. (Toto je len "
"orientačné pravidlo, ako všetky pravidlá vo videu — sú určené na to, aby sa "
"porušovali.)"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:76
msgid ""
"Also, some additional problems may arise due to the sensor being read out "
"line-wise. One I would like to mention are Rolling Shutter effects. Longer "
"exposure can, but need not, prevent such problems. It does if you are "
"shooting with fluorescent lamps. Shooting at high shutter speed shows wave "
"patterns from top to bottom of the screen, lowering it hides them if you hit "
"the correct shutter speed."
msgstr ""
"Tiež môžu nastať niektoré ďalšie problémy v dôsledku čítania snímača po "
"riadkoch. Jedným z nich, ktorý by som rád spomenul, je efekt rolujúcej "
"uzávierky (Rolling Shutter). Dlhšia expozícia môže, ale nemusí, zabrániť "
"takýmto problémom. Pomôže to, ak natáčate pri žiarivkách. Natáčanie pri "
"vysokej rýchlosti uzávierky zobrazuje vlnové vzory od vrchu po spodok "
"obrazovky, ich zníženie ich skryje, ak nastavíte správnu rýchlosť uzávierky."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:78
msgid ""
"On the right: Two images shot with the Nikon D90 of the author, the left one "
"at lowest ISO possible, the right one at highest possible."
msgstr ""
"Vpravo: Dve snímky nasnímaná s Nikon D90 autora, ľavá pri najnižšom možnom "
"ISO, pravá pri najvyššom možnom."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:81
msgid "Exposure"
msgstr "Expozícia"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:83
msgid "|pic5|  |pic6|"
msgstr "|pic5|  |pic6|"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:85
msgid "pic5"
msgstr "pic5"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:88
msgid "pic6"
msgstr "pic6"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:91
msgid ""
"The image should be exposed as bright as possible (without too much "
"clipping!) if enough light is available. If you do not need to boost the "
"brightness too much in post-production, you can avoid some noise in dark "
"areas."
msgstr ""
"Snímka by mala byť exponovaná čo najjasnejšie (bez nadmerného orezu!), ak je "
"k dispozícii dostatok svetla. Ak nepotrebujete príliš zvyšovať jas pri "
"postprodukcii, môžete sa vyhnúť šumu v tmavých oblastiach."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:94
msgid "White Balance"
msgstr "Vyváženie bielej"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:96
msgid "|pic7|  |pic8|"
msgstr "|pic7|  |pic8|"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:98
msgid "pic7"
msgstr "pic7"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:101
msgid "pic8"
msgstr "pic8"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:104
msgid ""
"The White Balance should be set as accurate as possible because DSLRs only "
"support 8 bit per color channel (see also the chapter about the :doc:"
"`Waveform Monitor </tips_and_tricks/scopes/waveform_and_rgb_parade>`). If "
"done wrong, much of the color information is lost."
msgstr ""
"Vyváženie bielej farby by malo byť nastavené čo najpresnejšie, pretože DSLR "
"fotoaparáty podporujú iba 8 bitov na farebný kanál (pozri tiež kapitolu o :"
"doc:`Waveform Monitor </tips_and_tricks/scopes/waveform_and_rgb_parade>`). "
"Ak je nastavené nesprávne, stratí sa veľká časť farebných informácií."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:106
msgid ""
"DSLRs also offer different camera profiles with different contrast, "
"saturation and other settings. Usually low saturation is preferred over high "
"saturation — especially because raising the saturation can be done in post, "
"and because high in-camera saturation settings can lead to color clipping."
msgstr ""
"DSLR fotoaparáty tiež ponúkajú rôzne profily fotoaparátu s rôznym "
"kontrastom, sýtosťou a inými nastaveniami. Zvyčajne sa uprednostňuje nízka "
"sýtosť pred vysokou — najmä preto, že zvyšovanie sýtosti je možné vykonať "
"pri postprodukcii, a pretože vysoké nastavenia sýtosti v samotnom "
"fotoaparáte môžu viesť k orezaniu farieb."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:108
msgid ""
"In the example images on the right you can see the difference. The left one "
"looked blueish due to wrong white balance and was corrected in post; much of "
"the tonal range of the blue colors has been lost. The right one has been "
"shot with proper white balance."
msgstr ""
"Na vzorových obrázkoch vpravo vidíte rozdiel. Ľavý vyzeral namodralý kvôli "
"nesprávnemu vyváženiu bielej a bol opravený pri postprodukcii; veľká časť "
"tónového rozsahu modrých farieb sa stratila. Pravý bol nasnímaný so správnym "
"vyvážením bielej."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:111
msgid "Autofocus"
msgstr "Autofokus"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:113
msgid ""
"The in-camera autofocus may be fast enough to focus, but it will fail in the "
"most important moment. It is useful for getting the initial focus point, but "
"while shooting it should stay switched off."
msgstr ""
"Automatické zaostrovanie vo fotoaparáte môže byť dostatočne rýchle na "
"zaostrenie, ale v tom najdôležitejšom momente zlyhá. Je užitočné na získanie "
"počiatočného bodu zaostrenia, ale počas natáčania by malo zostať vypnuté."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:117
msgid "Camera Specific Tips"
msgstr "Tipy špecifické pre fotoaparát"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:120
msgid "Nikon D90"
msgstr "Nikon D90"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:130
msgid ""
"The Nikon D90 was the first DSLR offering video: 720/24p (:abbr:`AVI (Audio "
"Video Interleave)` container)."
msgstr ""
"Nikon D90 bol prvý DSLR ponúkajúci video: 720/24p (kontajner :abbr:`AVI "
"(Audio Video Interleave)`)."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:132
msgid ""
"D90 videos at 720p are scaled awfully. That is why you can see stair-"
"stepping in sharp, skew lines. If this becomes perturbing for a clip, you "
"can apply the :doc:`/effects_and_filters/video_effects/utility/"
"nikon_d90_stairstepping_fix` filter. Written (but not invented) by the "
"original author *Granjow*. See our |nikon-d90| for an example of how "
"stairstepping looks like (before and after correction)."
msgstr ""
"Videá z D90 pri 720p sú hrozne škálované. Preto môžete vidieť schodíkový "
"efekt v ostrých, šikmých líniách. Ak sa toto stane pre klip rušivým, môžete "
"použiť filter :doc:`/effects_and_filters/video_effects/utility/"
"nikon_d90_stairstepping_fix`. Napísal (ale nevymyslel) pôvodný autor "
"*Granjow*. Pozrite si naše |nikon-d90| pre príklad toho, ako schodíkový "
"efekt vyzerá (pred a po korekcii)."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:134
msgid ""
"There is an extensive overview over the D90 video function at dvxuser.com: |"
"movie_mode|."
msgstr "Na dvxuser.com je rozsiahly prehľad funkcie videa D90: |movie_mode|."

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:138
msgid "Canon EOS 550D/Ti2 (and Co.)"
msgstr "Canon EOS 550D/Ti2 (a spol.)"

#: ../../tips_and_tricks/shooting_tips/shooting_with_your_DSLR.rst:140
msgid ""
"These cameras shoot 1080p (H.264 encoded, MOV container) — but record video "
"with a height of 1088 pixels. Prior to MLT 0.5.6 you have/had to crop the "
"additional 8 pixels with a crop effect from the top or the bottom of the "
"video, newer versions of MLT do this automatically."
msgstr ""
"Tieto fotoaparáty natáčajú 1080p (kódovanie H.264, kontajner MOV) — ale "
"zaznamenávajú video s výškou 1088 pixelov. Pred MLT 0.5.6 ste museli/musite "
"orezať ďalších 8 pixelov efektom orezania z vrchu alebo zo spodku videa, "
"novšie verzie MLT to robia automaticky."

